//
// Mesh level O1 -- G2-fluid domain built natively with blockMesh.
//
// Domain : anterior chamber + posterior chamber + pupil + trabecular meshwork
//          + vitreous, revolved 90 deg about +y (quarter calotte).
//          Lens and iris are VOIDS (walls). Cornea / sclera / choroid /
//          retina / ciliary body are solids and are not meshed.
//
// Geometry: Missel (2012) / Lamminsalo (2018) ESM Tables SI-SII, rabbit eye.
//          Table units are cm; here everything is written in MILLIMETRES and
//          converted by "scale 0.001".  Missel X -> x (radial), Missel Z -> y
//          (optical axis, + posterior).  y = 0 is the ellipsoid centre.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Analytic surfaces (Table SI, cm -> mm)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   cornea_inside    circle  centre (0, -0.15)  R = 8.01
//   lens_front       circle  centre (0, -0.31)  R = 5.76
//   lens_rear        circle  centre (0, -4.15)  R = 4.79
//   hyaloid_curved   circle  centre (0, +2.95)  R = 9.41
//   vitreous_retina  ellipse R1 = 8.37 (x), R2 = 6.90 (y), centred (0,0)
//
// All four circles are centred ON the revolve axis, so every circular
// meridional edge is written as "arc ... origin (0 yc 0)" -- exact, and valid
// unchanged in all three theta layers.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Meridional block corners
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Table SI/SII landmarks, used verbatim:
//   A  (0    , -8.16)   cornea inner apex                       [axis]
//   B  (6.61 , -4.68)   inner_sclera_cornea
//   C  (6.70 , -4.75)   tm_cornea_void
//   D  (6.93 , -4.49)   tm_ciliary_void
//   E  (6.84 , -4.42)   ciliary_tm_aqueous_sclera
//   F  (6.90 , -4.02)   iris_ciliary_ant
//   G  (6.92 , -3.86)   iris_ciliary_post
//   H  (7.00 , -3.35)   hyaloid_curved_flat (ciliary tip)
//   I  (8.01 , -2.00)   hyaloid_retina (ora); lies on BOTH the ellipse and
//                       the hyaloid circle, with an 11.6 deg tangent kink
//   J  (0    , +6.90)   posterior pole                          [axis]
//   K  (0    , +0.64)   lens rear apex                          [axis]
//   L  (4.75 , -3.57)   lens_eq_hyaloid (lens equator)
//   M  (0    , -6.07)   lens front apex                         [axis]
//   N  (3.78 , -4.94)   iris_turn_ant
//   O  (3.11 , -5.38)   iris_tip_ant
//   P  (3.00 , -5.27)   iris_tip_post
//   Q  (3.69 , -4.81)   iris_turn_post
//
// Derived corners (evaluated from the circles above):
//   R  (3.00 , -5.2270723)  foot of P on lens_front; face P-R is the pupil
//                           throat, 42.93 um.  NB the true minimum iris-lens
//                           clearance is 37.3 um at x = 3.195, which sits
//                           INSIDE block PCi -- see the gap function below.
//   T  (3.11 , -7.5315989)  cornea at the iris-tip radius
//   U  (3.78 , -7.2119900)  cornea at the iris-turn radius
//   V  (0    , -7.00)       axis station, also the ACP needle site   [axis]
//   V2 (0    , -7.60)       axis station                             [axis]
//   Z  (6.075475, -4.26313)  on the iris anterior segment F-N.
//       The peripheral AC is the pentagon B-E-F-N-U, and B is a REFLEX
//       corner: the cornea arrives with tangent 55.613 deg and the TM inner
//       face B-E leaves at 48.513 deg, so the fluid turns through 187.10 deg
//       there.  Any single block corner at B is therefore concave whatever
//       the cell size (this showed up as 36 concave cells, 24 mis-oriented
//       face pyramids and skewness 233 in the first attempt).  The pentagon
//       is instead cut from B along the bisector of that reflex angle
//       (142.060 deg) to Z on F-N, giving two convex quads with 93.55 deg
//       each at B.  This also removes the collapsed iris-root fan block: the
//       65.05 deg corner at F is now an ordinary hex corner, so the only
//       prisms left in the mesh are the four axis-touching blocks.
//   Y  (5.21718, -4.36082941)  on the iris posterior segment Q-G.
//       The obvious posterior-chamber cut L-Q cannot be used: its midpoint
//       (4.22, -4.189) is 29 um INSIDE the lens_front sphere, so a block
//       bounded by both the lens arc R-L and the chord L-Q self-intersects,
//       and the corner it leaves at L is only 6.5 deg.  Instead the 130.03
//       deg fluid corner at L (between the lens_front tangent, 235.557 deg,
//       and the chord L-H, 5.583 deg) is BISECTED: the ray leaving L at
//       300.570 deg meets the line Q-G at Y, giving 65.01 deg on each side.
//       Q itself survives as an interior point of the polyLine iris edge
//       P-Q-Y, so the Table SII iris polygon is still exact.
//
// Vitreous subdivision, 6 internal cuts (needed for the theta accuracy
// argument below).  Shell stations on the ellipse, x = 8.37 sin t,
// y = 6.90 cos t:
//   S1 t = 18 deg, S2 t = 36, S3 t = 54, S4 t = 72, S5 t = 90, then I at
//   t = 106.85 deg.  Lens-rear stations W1..W6 at phi = k*83.038543/7 deg,
//   x = 4.79 sin phi, y = -4.15 + 4.79 cos phi.
//
// Iris-lens clearance (iris posterior P-Q is straight, lens front is a
// circle):   gap(x) = 6.96 - 0.66667 x - sqrt(33.1776 - x^2)  [mm]
//   x = 3.000 -> 42.93 um (tip corner P)
//   x = 3.195 -> 37.34 um (MINIMUM)
//   x = 3.690 -> 77.16 um (turning point Q)
// Block PCi spans this gap in its x1 direction with 8 cells everywhere, so
// the minimum section is resolved by 8 cells of ~4.7 um.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Why 2 theta blocks and 7 vitreous blocks
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// blockMesh builds block interiors by transfinite interpolation from the 12
// edges, so a swept surface of revolution is only reproduced exactly where
// the meridional edge is straight.  For a block spanning dTheta the radial
// error at mid-sweep is
//       err = (1 - cos(dTheta/2)) * (r_chord - r_true)
// i.e. the coefficient times the chord deviation of the meridional edge.
// One 90 deg block over the whole shell would pinch the retina inward by
// 0.93 mm.  With dTheta = 45 deg (coeff 0.0761) and the shell cut into six
// ~18 deg pieces (deviation ~0.21 mm) the worst surface error is ~16 um,
// below the ~40 um self-consistency of Tables SI-SII themselves.  The same
// subdivision makes every shell segment an exact 3-point arc (ellipse-to-arc
// error < 1 um over 18 deg).
//
// Vertex layers: 0-26 theta = 0, 27-53 theta = 45, 54-80 theta = 90,
// 81-86 on the axis (shared by all layers -> the four axis-touching blocks
// are collapsed hexes, i.e. prisms).
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       dictionary;
    object      blockMeshDict;
}
// * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * //

scale   0.001;      // vertices in mm

vertices
(
    // ---------------- layer 0 : theta = 0 deg  (x, y, 0) ----------------
    (6.61       -4.68        0)              //  0  B
    (6.70       -4.75        0)              //  1  C
    (6.93       -4.49        0)              //  2  D
    (6.84       -4.42        0)              //  3  E
    (6.90       -4.02        0)              //  4  F
    (6.92       -3.86        0)              //  5  G
    (7.00       -3.35        0)              //  6  H
    (4.75       -3.57        0)              //  7  L
    (3.78       -4.94        0)              //  8  N
    (3.11       -5.38        0)              //  9  O
    (3.00       -5.27        0)              // 10  P
    (5.21718    -4.36082941  0)              // 11  Y   bisector cut on Q-G
    (3.00       -5.2270723   0)              // 12  R
    (3.11       -7.5315989   0)              // 13  T
    (3.78       -7.2119900   0)              // 14  U
    (2.58647221  6.56228999  0)              // 15  S1  ellipse t=18
    (4.91976254  5.58221723  0)              // 16  S2  ellipse t=36
    (6.77147221  4.05571823  0)              // 17  S3  ellipse t=54
    (7.96034307  2.13221723  0)              // 18  S4  ellipse t=72
    (8.37        0.0         0)              // 19  S5  ellipse t=90
    (8.01       -2.00        0)              // 20  I   ora
    (0.98466162  0.53770000  0)              // 21  W1  lens rear
    (1.92726600  0.23517400  0)              // 22  W2
    (2.78754500 -0.25466200  0)              // 23  W3
    (3.52877400 -0.91087800  0)              // 24  W4
    (4.11925900 -1.70545300  0)              // 25  W5
    (4.53380010 -2.60443900  0)              // 26  W6

    // ---------------- layer 1 : theta = 45 deg  (x/sqrt2, y, x/sqrt2) ---
    (4.67397582 -4.68        4.67397582)     // 27  B
    (4.73761543 -4.75        4.73761543)     // 28  C
    (4.90024999 -4.49        4.90024999)     // 29  D
    (4.83661038 -4.42        4.83661038)     // 30  E
    (4.87903678 -4.02        4.87903678)     // 31  F
    (4.89317892 -3.86        4.89317892)     // 32  G
    (4.94974746 -3.35        4.94974746)     // 33  H
    (3.35875721 -3.57        3.35875721)     // 34  L
    (2.67286363 -4.94        2.67286363)     // 35  N
    (2.19910209 -5.38        2.19910209)     // 36  O
    (2.12132034 -5.27        2.12132034)     // 37  P
    (3.68910336 -4.36082941  3.68910336)     // 38  Y
    (2.12132034 -5.2270723   2.12132034)     // 39  R
    (2.19910209 -7.5315989   2.19910209)     // 40  T
    (2.67286363 -7.2119900   2.67286363)     // 41  U
    (1.82891266  6.56228999  1.82891266)     // 42  S1
    (3.47879641  5.58221723  3.47879641)     // 43  S2
    (4.78815392  4.05571823  4.78815392)     // 44  S3
    (5.62881148  2.13221723  5.62881148)     // 45  S4
    (5.91848375  0.0         5.91848375)     // 46  S5
    (5.66392531 -2.00        5.66392531)     // 47  I
    (0.69626093  0.53770000  0.69626093)     // 48  W1
    (1.36278488  0.23517400  1.36278488)     // 49  W2
    (1.97108997 -0.25466200  1.97108997)     // 50  W3
    (2.49522201 -0.91087800  2.49522201)     // 51  W4
    (2.91275524 -1.70545300  2.91275524)     // 52  W5
    (3.20588043 -2.60443900  3.20588043)     // 53  W6

    // ---------------- layer 2 : theta = 90 deg  (0, y, x) ---------------
    (0          -4.68        6.61      )     // 54  B
    (0          -4.75        6.70      )     // 55  C
